WEBVTT

00:07.382 --> 00:09.384
[opening theme music playing]

00:12.429 --> 00:14.431
[wind gusting]

00:37.787 --> 00:41.916
GYEONGSEONG CREATURE 2

00:42.000 --> 00:43.334
[music fades]

00:44.961 --> 00:47.005
[train horn wailing]

00:48.381 --> 00:50.383
[ethereal music playing]

00:58.183 --> 01:00.060
[automated voice] The doors are opening.

01:06.733 --> 01:09.194
[traffic noise]

01:09.277 --> 01:11.946
[phone ringing]

01:17.911 --> 01:20.497
[indistinct chattering]

01:20.580 --> 01:22.082
[dog barking in distance]

01:28.963 --> 01:30.965
[soothing jazz music playing]

01:39.974 --> 01:41.976
[siren wailing in distance]

01:47.065 --> 01:48.316
[soothing jazz music continues]

01:48.399 --> 01:49.651
Would you like to order, sir?

01:49.734 --> 01:51.945
Yes. So I, uh…

01:53.279 --> 01:57.200
I'm here to see someone
who goes by the name Silverbill.

01:58.076 --> 02:00.078
[motorcycle engine roaring]

02:01.704 --> 02:03.706
[tires squealing]

02:04.707 --> 02:06.084
[motorcycle engine roaring]

02:12.924 --> 02:15.176
- [glass shattering]
- [loud clattering]

02:16.636 --> 02:17.804
[car engine accelerates]

02:17.887 --> 02:19.055
[tires squealing]

02:21.141 --> 02:22.767
[shuddered breathing]

02:22.851 --> 02:28.022
It's been over… ten days
since I lost contact with my son.

02:28.106 --> 02:30.608
If your kid ran away,
you should go talk to the authorities.

02:30.692 --> 02:32.068
He didn't run away.

02:33.903 --> 02:35.363
- He has gone missing.
- [phone buzzing]

02:36.489 --> 02:38.658
MADAM NA

02:38.741 --> 02:39.868
[stirring music playing]

02:39.951 --> 02:41.077
[Madam Na] Job request.

02:41.161 --> 02:44.497
Missing person's name, Oh Ki-hoon.
29 years old.

02:45.206 --> 02:47.167
He went missing about ten days ago.

02:49.836 --> 02:50.753
Are you available?

02:52.338 --> 02:54.340
[dramatic music playing]

02:58.178 --> 03:00.180
[low thrumming sound]

03:01.181 --> 03:02.891
[metallic clattering]

03:11.316 --> 03:12.609
[music intensifies]

03:19.908 --> 03:21.492
- [slicing]
- [blood squelching]

03:21.576 --> 03:22.952
[blades rasping]

03:24.120 --> 03:25.914
- [engine roars]
- [loud thud]

03:32.503 --> 03:33.880
[music swells]

03:33.963 --> 03:35.632
[soothing piano music playing]

03:35.715 --> 03:38.384
ACCEPTED

03:47.310 --> 03:48.519
[music fades]

03:51.522 --> 03:53.524
[unsettling music playing]

04:17.674 --> 04:20.009
[dramatic music playing]

04:24.055 --> 04:26.224
[coughing, gasping]

04:28.142 --> 04:30.728
For how long were you planning
to keep this up?

04:34.899 --> 04:37.694
I think it's time
you forget everything, hmm?

04:39.404 --> 04:40.446
[scoffs]

04:41.155 --> 04:43.574
[coughing, gasps]

04:45.368 --> 04:46.536
[music swells]

04:46.619 --> 04:47.870
[music subsides]

04:48.746 --> 04:50.748
[mysterious music playing]

04:50.832 --> 04:51.833
[sighs]

04:53.710 --> 04:54.627
[sighs]

04:56.546 --> 04:57.672
[sighs]

04:58.464 --> 05:02.385
GYEONGSEONG CREATURE
BETWEEN AWARENESS AND BLINDNESS

05:03.678 --> 05:04.679
[sighs]

05:18.109 --> 05:19.986
[inhales]

05:20.737 --> 05:22.030
[exhales]

05:24.115 --> 05:27.243
[phone buzzing]

05:29.620 --> 05:31.831
Yes, Jang Ho-jae of Bugang Company.

05:32.874 --> 05:36.794
EPISODE 1
HO-JAE

05:36.878 --> 05:40.131
BUGANG COMPANY
PIONEER OF GLOBAL COMMERCE

05:40.214 --> 05:42.800
BUGANG COMPANY
THE CENTER OF TRADE IN ASIA

05:42.884 --> 05:45.762
THE PRIDE OF JONGNO RETURNS ANEW

05:45.845 --> 05:49.891
CALL FOR ANY AND ALL REQUESTS
ON-CALL 24/7

05:49.974 --> 05:51.976
[melodic acoustic guitar music playing]

05:53.853 --> 05:55.772
[blows, slurps]

05:55.855 --> 05:56.898
Mmm.

05:57.690 --> 05:58.608
Mmm.

06:00.777 --> 06:01.694
Where are you going?

06:01.778 --> 06:04.364
I think we can grab the evidence
Mr. Yang requested, so I'm on it.

06:04.447 --> 06:05.531
Wait a minute. Hold on.

06:06.032 --> 06:09.869
You should've told me sooner. Jeez.
We gotta go together for that job.

06:09.952 --> 06:11.079
I thought you knew that.

06:11.162 --> 06:13.790
Yong-gil, but I'm in charge today.
All right?

06:14.332 --> 06:16.626
- Since when are you ever in charge, hmm?
- [scoffs]

06:16.709 --> 06:18.961
Let's not change tradition
if we don't have to.

06:19.045 --> 06:20.630
Winner gets to call the shots.

06:20.713 --> 06:21.714
Okay.

06:23.341 --> 06:24.300
Ready?

06:25.468 --> 06:28.137
- Cham cham cham!
- Cham cham cham!

06:28.221 --> 06:29.055
[Ho-jae sighs]

06:29.680 --> 06:30.807
[blows] I win.

06:31.432 --> 06:32.892
- Not fair.
- Mm-hmm.

06:33.476 --> 06:35.395
Since you're the loser,
I'll drive as well.

06:35.478 --> 06:36.437
Let's go.

06:37.230 --> 06:39.232
Cham cham cham. Cham cham cham.

06:39.315 --> 06:40.525
Why can't I do it?

06:43.611 --> 06:46.781
[scanner beeping]

06:47.407 --> 06:48.991
[cashier] Sixty-eight hundred won.

06:49.826 --> 06:51.411
[door chimes ringing]

06:51.494 --> 06:53.496
[uneasy music playing]

07:09.720 --> 07:11.305
[bag zipping]

07:11.389 --> 07:13.182
[Yong-gil sighs] Jeez.

07:13.266 --> 07:14.684
Hey, Ho-jae.

07:14.767 --> 07:17.603
You know we gotta pay off
the loan interest this week, right?

07:17.687 --> 07:20.106
If you can't get a clear photo
to use as evidence today,

07:20.815 --> 07:23.276
we won't get paid, and the creditors
will start coming for us.

07:23.943 --> 07:25.945
And before we can blink,
the office will get seized,

07:26.028 --> 07:27.488
and we'll be sleeping on the streets.

07:27.572 --> 07:30.658
Yong-gil, something I've always wondered.

07:30.741 --> 07:31.909
Yeah?

07:31.993 --> 07:33.953
The debt you've acquired
has nothing to do with me,

07:34.036 --> 07:35.663
so why do I have to help you pay it again?

07:35.746 --> 07:38.082
That's a good question. It's because, uh…

07:38.166 --> 07:41.669
Well, I am the president of Bugang,
and you are the vice president.

07:42.462 --> 07:43.504
Oh yeah? Since when?

07:43.588 --> 07:45.548
Here, put these on. Here.

07:48.384 --> 07:50.470
Hey, Bugang is an inheritance
from Grandpa.

07:50.553 --> 07:52.930
I mean, who else is gonna
protect the company if we don't?

07:53.014 --> 07:56.309
You, me, us.
We have to protect it together, all right?

07:58.227 --> 08:01.397
Strictly speaking, he's your grandpa.
Don't know how I got involved.

08:02.106 --> 08:04.442
Hey, you know how much
my grandpa loved you, right?

08:04.525 --> 08:06.569
Yes, you always say that,
but I don't remember.

08:06.652 --> 08:10.531
Also, don't forget the fact that you and I
got no place else to go besides Bugang.

08:10.615 --> 08:13.743
Hey, that's not true.
You know, I'm in really high demand.

08:14.994 --> 08:16.579
Cham cham… cham.

08:17.747 --> 08:19.040
I'm in charge. Here.

08:19.916 --> 08:22.585
Take this and go. We don't have all night.
Don't let 'em see you.

08:22.668 --> 08:24.879
Go, go, go. Hurry. Get going.

08:25.922 --> 08:27.089
Come on!

08:27.173 --> 08:28.799
You didn't get their faces last time.

08:28.883 --> 08:30.510
- Get the faces.
- Blah, blah, blah, blah.

08:30.593 --> 08:32.845
[Yong-gil] If the angle sucks,
we get half the pay!

08:33.346 --> 08:34.680
Love you, Vice President!

08:35.348 --> 08:37.934
Remember, don't just get the body.
Get the whole face.

08:38.768 --> 08:39.727
[sighs]

08:41.229 --> 08:43.231
[stirring music playing]

08:45.608 --> 08:47.068
[door chimes ringing]

09:05.920 --> 09:07.004
[elevator bell dings]

09:08.172 --> 09:09.590
[music fades]

09:19.267 --> 09:20.268
[door lock clicks]

09:35.116 --> 09:37.118
[TV playing indistinctly]

09:47.253 --> 09:49.005
[can opens]

09:50.881 --> 09:51.882
[sighs]

09:53.467 --> 09:55.469
[gulping]

09:57.638 --> 09:58.639
[sighs]

10:03.728 --> 10:05.730
[unsettling music playing]

10:10.359 --> 10:11.569
[distant clatter]

10:20.077 --> 10:21.287
Is someone there?

10:37.261 --> 10:39.263
[tense music playing]

10:52.568 --> 10:53.736
[breathing nervously]

10:55.946 --> 10:58.949
- [music fades]
- [breathing heavily]

11:00.826 --> 11:01.702
[sighs]

11:04.914 --> 11:06.082
[TV shuts off]

11:08.626 --> 11:10.628
[breathing nervously]

11:10.711 --> 11:12.713
[unsettling music playing]

11:18.135 --> 11:20.137
[breathing nervously]

11:24.558 --> 11:26.977
[skin tearing]

11:29.855 --> 11:31.399
[music fades]

11:36.862 --> 11:38.447
You're getting the feed, right?

11:39.615 --> 11:42.034
Of course I am.
I'm the one who made it, huh?

12:13.190 --> 12:14.817
[Yong-gil] Why isn't anyone answering?

12:15.609 --> 12:16.777
They must be preoccupied, huh?

12:16.861 --> 12:18.654
Hey, stop. Don't do that. Sheesh.

12:18.738 --> 12:20.781
You sure room 608 is the right one?

12:22.450 --> 12:23.868
Yeah, I'm positive.

12:24.452 --> 12:25.911
It's room 608.

12:29.290 --> 12:31.292
[mysterious music playing]

12:49.351 --> 12:51.604
I really don't have
a good feeling about this.

12:51.687 --> 12:53.063
Should we call it quits?

12:53.147 --> 12:55.191
Ho-jae, we need this. All right?

12:55.274 --> 12:57.818
We have to pay off the interest
this week. I told you.

12:57.902 --> 12:59.570
Otherwise, we get evicted, remember?

13:00.404 --> 13:03.157
We don't have a choice.
We've gotta get the evidence today.

13:03.240 --> 13:05.242
[mysterious music continues]

13:22.843 --> 13:24.929
[Yong-gil] Hey, just barge in there, okay?

13:25.012 --> 13:27.598
You have the master key I gave you, right?
Open the door with that.

13:27.681 --> 13:30.559
And just take one picture. That's it.
Then you're done, huh?

13:31.393 --> 13:32.269
[Yong-gil groans]

13:32.353 --> 13:34.939
- For heaven's sake.
- Ho-jae, please. Please. Just do it.

13:45.825 --> 13:47.827
[music intensifies]

13:51.205 --> 13:52.248
[music subsides]

13:58.671 --> 13:59.505
[exhales]

14:00.548 --> 14:02.550
[unsettling music playing]

14:08.556 --> 14:09.849
[Ho-jae] There's no one here.

14:09.932 --> 14:13.060
Bathroom. Check the bathroom.
They might be taking a shower together.

14:15.229 --> 14:17.106
[unsettling music continues]

14:25.030 --> 14:26.740
[door hinges creaking]

14:28.117 --> 14:28.951
Oh shit!

14:32.621 --> 14:33.873
[loud clattering]

14:33.956 --> 14:35.875
What the-- Ho-jae?

14:36.959 --> 14:38.335
[Ho-jae groans]

14:38.419 --> 14:40.170
[mysterious music playing]

14:46.844 --> 14:47.761
[loud thud]

14:47.845 --> 14:48.888
[Ho-jae grunts]

14:51.891 --> 14:53.934
Is that… a woman?

14:54.894 --> 14:56.312
[Ho-jae grunting]

14:57.021 --> 14:58.022
- [thud]
- [Ho-jae grunts]

14:59.481 --> 15:01.442
[grunting]

15:02.234 --> 15:04.486
- [phone clatters]
- [Ho-jae coughing, gasping]

15:05.362 --> 15:06.280
[glasses clatter]

15:06.363 --> 15:08.157
- Huh? Oh!
- [Ho-jae coughing]

15:10.117 --> 15:12.077
[tense music playing]

15:15.122 --> 15:16.040
Oh shit!

15:16.916 --> 15:19.001
- Sir! Something's wrong in room 608!
- What?

15:19.084 --> 15:21.170
- Hurry, sir! Hurry up! Come on!
- What's going on?

15:26.091 --> 15:27.384
[tense music continues]

15:28.552 --> 15:29.887
- [bones crack]
- [grunts]

15:32.222 --> 15:34.224
[Ho-jae coughing]

15:38.854 --> 15:40.314
[Ho-jae panting]

15:46.779 --> 15:47.780
[Ho-jae] Hey!

15:59.249 --> 16:01.335
- [footsteps approaching]
- [door opens]

16:02.419 --> 16:03.712
[Yong-gil] Ho-jae, I'm here!

16:03.796 --> 16:04.713
- Ho-jae.
- Yong-gil.

16:04.797 --> 16:06.507
[man 1 screams, whimpers]

16:07.883 --> 16:08.968
I, uh…

16:10.803 --> 16:12.012
[Yong-gil] Oh shit.

16:12.096 --> 16:13.764
[panting]

16:14.348 --> 16:16.433
- What the--
- What are you two doing?

16:16.517 --> 16:17.851
[music fades]

16:17.935 --> 16:20.646
- What are you doing in here?
- You wrote down 608.

16:20.729 --> 16:23.524
No, I did not. I wrote 809.

16:31.907 --> 16:33.575
Ah shit.

16:35.828 --> 16:37.663
Oh shit.

16:39.081 --> 16:41.208
[unsettling music playing]

16:48.257 --> 16:49.967
[upbeat jazz music playing]

16:50.050 --> 16:51.218
[phone buzzing]

16:57.683 --> 16:58.851
DESERTER ELIMINATED

17:01.729 --> 17:02.688
[woman] Honey.

17:06.650 --> 17:08.986
DESERTER ELIMINATED

17:09.778 --> 17:11.780
[unsettling music playing]

17:15.909 --> 17:17.911
[reverential music playing]

17:43.353 --> 17:46.273
[camera shutter clicking]

17:46.356 --> 17:48.108
[dramatic music playing]

17:48.192 --> 17:50.444
[sobbing]

17:56.575 --> 17:59.078
[music swells to crescendo]

17:59.912 --> 18:01.914
I'm telling you, she was a total pro.

18:01.997 --> 18:05.167
I mean, she knew how to fight,
position her shoulders, everything.

18:05.250 --> 18:06.877
And what else do you remember?

18:06.960 --> 18:09.046
Hey, I already told you everything.

18:09.129 --> 18:11.173
It was pitch-black.
I could barely see at all.

18:11.256 --> 18:14.218
And she kept throwing punches
over and over and then--

18:14.301 --> 18:15.219
[grunts]

18:15.302 --> 18:17.679
[eerie music stab plays]

18:19.807 --> 18:21.183
That's everything.

18:21.266 --> 18:22.976
What were you thinking, Ho-jae?

18:24.311 --> 18:27.815
Without any evidence to corroborate
your story, you will take the fall.

18:28.357 --> 18:31.235
- Hmm? What do you mean?
- Are you serious?

18:31.318 --> 18:33.529
You were trying to catch
two people having an affair,

18:33.612 --> 18:35.155
but it all backfired in the end.

18:35.239 --> 18:36.949
It resulted in a fight
between the parties.

18:37.032 --> 18:37.950
One ended up dead.

18:38.033 --> 18:39.243
- No!
- Hey, that's not true!

18:39.326 --> 18:41.078
The only fingerprints
we found at the scene

18:41.161 --> 18:42.538
were your fingerprints, Mr. Jang.

18:42.621 --> 18:45.207
I told you that guy was already dead.
This is unfair.

18:45.290 --> 18:47.417
The victim's blood
was also found all over your clothes.

18:47.501 --> 18:48.460
How do you explain that?

18:48.544 --> 18:51.922
Because I was fighting with the woman,
and she threw me all around the scene.

18:52.005 --> 18:54.049
Yes, exactly. I witnessed it on video.

18:54.133 --> 18:55.968
Ho-jae was getting his ass
handed to him by her.

18:56.051 --> 18:57.469
- Right?
- Shut up.

18:57.553 --> 18:59.721
Okay, but he's not the type of person
to kill someone.

18:59.805 --> 19:01.974
I swear to you, Captain Yuh.
See? I got you.

19:02.057 --> 19:05.394
I told you guys to stop fooling around
with all this private detective business.

19:05.477 --> 19:06.353
Didn't I?

19:06.436 --> 19:08.814
How many times have I told you
to stop wiretapping people

19:08.897 --> 19:10.732
and recording people
without their consent?

19:10.816 --> 19:11.650
It's against the law.

19:11.733 --> 19:13.694
Yes, you did.
You told us all this, Captain Yuh.

19:13.777 --> 19:15.904
Look at this. Look. This is blackmail.

19:16.738 --> 19:19.700
All of these pictures you have are illegal
and taken without their consent.

19:19.783 --> 19:21.451
All people caught in the act.

19:21.535 --> 19:24.121
I can barely look at these.
I'm so embarrassed for them.

19:24.204 --> 19:26.165
Coming from the person
who keeps looking at them.

19:26.248 --> 19:27.541
Hey!

19:27.624 --> 19:28.917
You give me no choice.

19:29.585 --> 19:32.546
You both will have to be locked up
on illegal filming charges for this.

19:32.629 --> 19:35.424
Hold your horses.
That's extreme, don't you think?

19:35.507 --> 19:36.967
Why are you doing this to us?

19:37.467 --> 19:38.969
You know how it's been.

19:39.052 --> 19:41.346
In the beginning, see, we, um…

19:41.430 --> 19:44.308
we started out in commerce and trade
in the global market.

19:44.391 --> 19:46.268
Although, in this worldwide
economic recession,

19:46.351 --> 19:49.021
tiny companies like us
have been crushed down to dust.

19:49.104 --> 19:51.231
We're just trying
to put food on the table.

19:51.315 --> 19:55.402
That's all it is. So we got into
a little side hustle very, very briefly.

19:55.485 --> 19:57.112
But you know us, Captain.

19:57.196 --> 19:58.447
[laughs] You know us.

19:58.530 --> 19:59.573
[laughs]

20:03.535 --> 20:06.246
I'll be quiet now
so you two can continue talking.

20:09.291 --> 20:10.751
Let's stop the charade, okay?

20:11.335 --> 20:12.377
Tell me what this is about.

20:13.587 --> 20:14.630
What?

20:14.713 --> 20:18.050
It's pretty obvious you're just trying
to scare us with these charges.

20:18.133 --> 20:20.135
You must want something from us here.

20:20.969 --> 20:22.387
So tell me what it is you want.

20:32.856 --> 20:34.024
Find this person.

20:35.400 --> 20:36.235
- Huh?
- What?

20:36.318 --> 20:37.653
You can't be serious.

20:37.736 --> 20:39.655
Wait, the police should--

20:39.738 --> 20:42.282
Shouldn't you be looking for the criminal?
Why would we help?

20:42.366 --> 20:46.370
We already arrested our key suspects,
but you said that this is unfair, so…

20:46.453 --> 20:48.580
If you really feel that way,
then help us out.

20:48.664 --> 20:50.499
A word, Captain Yuh?

20:50.582 --> 20:52.834
Captain, please. This is a little bit--

20:52.918 --> 20:54.753
[Captain Yuh] What? You can't do it?

20:54.836 --> 20:56.129
That's fine.

20:56.213 --> 20:58.507
Jang Ho-jae, you can just
stay right where you are

20:58.590 --> 21:00.509
as the prime suspect in this murder.

21:00.592 --> 21:03.387
Pretty soon, your name and face
will get plastered all over the news.

21:03.470 --> 21:04.304
You'll be famous.

21:04.388 --> 21:06.515
I told you I didn't kill anyone!

21:06.598 --> 21:08.767
That's what I'm trying
to tell you right now.

21:08.850 --> 21:12.396
If you didn't do it, find out who did,
or you'll take the fall.

21:12.479 --> 21:14.898
In the end, I still have a case to solve.

21:14.982 --> 21:16.984
The person who was
at the scene of the crime

21:17.067 --> 21:18.694
when the victim was murdered was you.

21:18.777 --> 21:21.530
So, currently,
the prime suspect is you, okay?

21:22.030 --> 21:22.906
You do your part,

21:22.990 --> 21:25.367
and we'll revise our report
before anyone sees it.

21:28.328 --> 21:30.580
Well, Captain Yuh, I'll have you know

21:30.664 --> 21:31.832
you really suck

21:32.833 --> 21:34.001
at your job there, buddy.

21:34.084 --> 21:35.544
Well, you're one to talk.

21:37.546 --> 21:40.757
I'll give you ten days.
Find whatever leads you can for now.

21:40.841 --> 21:43.468
Who the person is.
If it's really a woman or a man.

21:43.552 --> 21:46.888
And what kind of psycho they have to be
to go around killing like this.

21:46.972 --> 21:50.475
If you can't do it, just tell me.
I'll go ahead and arrest you now.

21:50.559 --> 21:51.768
What will it be?

21:54.354 --> 21:55.480
[Ho-jae sighs]

21:56.648 --> 21:58.650
[mysterious music playing]

22:02.154 --> 22:03.447
[Yong-gil sighs]

22:06.575 --> 22:10.662
Ho-jae, we're really screwed
with this whole thing, aren't we? Right?

22:12.622 --> 22:15.250
[woman] Are you sure this is okay?
They're both civilians.

22:17.669 --> 22:19.838
How can they go up
against a serial killer?

22:19.921 --> 22:22.424
Remember that creep we nabbed
about two months ago?

22:23.050 --> 22:25.218
You had just transferred
to the Violent Crimes Unit.

22:25.302 --> 22:27.971
The sex offender
who targeted female college students?

22:28.055 --> 22:29.765
The pain in your neck
for over three years?

22:29.848 --> 22:32.684
Mm-hmm. Those two found the guy.

22:33.352 --> 22:34.186
What?

22:34.269 --> 22:37.564
The guy, Jang Ho-jae?
He's way better than he lets on.

22:39.149 --> 22:40.525
So don't worry about them.

22:40.609 --> 22:43.153
[mysterious music playing]

22:43.236 --> 22:45.822
JONGNO-GU SERIAL MURDER CASE

22:53.205 --> 22:57.626
OH KI-HOON (29 YEARS OLD)
BODYGUARD AT JEONSEUNG BIOTECH

22:57.709 --> 22:58.627
[music fades]

22:58.710 --> 23:00.420
[owner] We haven't opened yet, sir.

23:04.883 --> 23:06.551
How can I help you this time?

23:06.635 --> 23:10.138
Your… your contact, Silverbill,
I want to meet them now.

23:11.056 --> 23:13.934
Sir, what happened to your son
was quite unfortunate,

23:14.017 --> 23:15.644
but there was nothing we could do for him.

23:17.437 --> 23:20.315
I've refunded your deposit. It should be
in your account in a few days.

23:20.399 --> 23:22.984
There's no need. Cancel the transfer.

23:23.693 --> 23:24.528
Sir?

23:24.611 --> 23:27.239
I wanna hire the Silverbill
to look for someone.

23:28.281 --> 23:29.199
Who were you thinking?

23:29.282 --> 23:31.660
Find whoever killed my son for me.

23:32.327 --> 23:35.205
Whatever it takes.
I want him to face justice for this.

23:35.789 --> 23:36.623
Please!

23:41.336 --> 23:42.629
[Madam Na] So what do you think?

23:43.880 --> 23:45.841
The client wants you
to find whoever killed his son

23:45.924 --> 23:47.467
by whatever means necessary.

23:47.551 --> 23:49.553
[wistful music playing]

24:14.453 --> 24:15.579
Ho-jae, listen.

24:16.079 --> 24:19.332
Why don't we leave Seoul for a bit
instead of doing this, huh?

24:19.416 --> 24:21.293
How about Osaka? Or Singapore.

24:21.376 --> 24:23.879
Or should we just book it to Hawaii?

24:24.546 --> 24:27.048
Have you considered the possibility
that traveling abroad

24:27.132 --> 24:28.925
might make it look as though
I am the culprit?

24:29.009 --> 24:30.677
Do you want me
to be a globally wanted man?

24:30.760 --> 24:32.846
No, that's not what I meant at all.

24:32.929 --> 24:34.222
What I'm trying to say is that

24:34.306 --> 24:36.641
we should get away
from the danger for a while.

24:36.725 --> 24:38.477
What if you end up
getting hurt in all this?

24:39.936 --> 24:41.188
You got money to go to Hawaii?

24:41.771 --> 24:44.232
No, of course I don't.
We'll find a way though.

24:44.941 --> 24:47.360
Listen, in times like this,
you can't run away.

24:47.444 --> 24:49.237
You've gotta find a way through it.

24:49.821 --> 24:51.740
Let's be practical for once.

24:51.823 --> 24:54.409
What does that even mean "be practical?"
This is a murder case.

24:54.493 --> 24:56.828
You actually think you're gonna
find the killer or something?

24:58.038 --> 24:58.914
What's this for?

24:59.623 --> 25:02.083
Let's start by sharing that photo
with all of our informants.

25:02.751 --> 25:06.505
Tell them to be on the lookout for anyone
who looks like the woman in the photo.

25:07.839 --> 25:09.299
Ho-jae, are you really doing this?

25:09.382 --> 25:10.884
The other option is that, in ten days,

25:10.967 --> 25:13.470
everyone in the country
will think I am the killer.

25:14.679 --> 25:17.557
I'd rather live a quiet life, my friend.

25:18.850 --> 25:20.018
Help me out, all right?

25:21.269 --> 25:22.103
[sighs]

25:28.401 --> 25:29.361
[sighs]

25:31.988 --> 25:32.822
[sighs]

25:35.075 --> 25:36.034
[exhales]

25:39.704 --> 25:40.914
[wistful music playing]

25:41.540 --> 25:45.418
Hey, Grandpa, why did you
ask me for this favor, huh?

25:50.090 --> 25:53.593
HELLO ANTENNAS, REQUESTING TIP-OFFS
ON THE PERSON IN THE PICTURE

25:58.848 --> 26:02.394
URGENTLY NEEDED, PLEASE CONTACT ASAP

26:02.978 --> 26:04.229
[phone chimes]

26:04.312 --> 26:05.397
[stirring music playing]

26:06.982 --> 26:08.024
[phone buzzing]

26:10.860 --> 26:13.113
- This is all so delicious.
- Did you bring that from home?

26:16.992 --> 26:18.743
- Hey, good work today.
- You as well.

26:18.827 --> 26:21.329
- [phone buzzing]
- I'm done. I should start heading out.

26:22.330 --> 26:23.456
- [man 1] Oh.
- [man 2] What?

26:23.540 --> 26:24.708
Have you seen this yet?

26:24.791 --> 26:26.084
Have I seen what yet?

26:35.176 --> 26:36.219
[music fades]

27:25.352 --> 27:27.354
[mysterious music playing]

27:45.914 --> 27:47.916
[melodic piano music playing]

28:21.449 --> 28:23.410
Ho-jae. Our guys in Sinsa-dong.

28:23.493 --> 28:25.578
They were taking pictures
of a building to quote a job,

28:25.662 --> 28:27.747
and they just happened
to see her standing there.

28:27.831 --> 28:30.417
They saw her multiple times
since then, so they say.

28:30.500 --> 28:32.419
Apparently, she appears
right before sunset

28:32.502 --> 28:34.671
and just sits there until it gets dark.

28:36.381 --> 28:37.424
Where in Sinsa-dong?

28:44.431 --> 28:46.266
[music intensifies]

29:03.199 --> 29:05.201
[music subsides]

29:17.839 --> 29:18.840
[phone buzzing]

29:19.674 --> 29:20.633
[music fades]

29:21.718 --> 29:23.219
ACCEPTED

29:23.303 --> 29:24.512
What?

29:26.014 --> 29:26.931
SILVERBILL

29:27.015 --> 29:28.475
[phone line ringing]

29:29.517 --> 29:31.227
- [call connects]
- You sure about this?

29:31.728 --> 29:33.438
You're really going to accept this job?

29:34.564 --> 29:35.732
Under one condition.

29:36.232 --> 29:39.110
Once I find him, I take him to the police.
No exceptions.

29:39.861 --> 29:42.822
Tell him that I don't take jobs
based on personal vengeance

29:43.656 --> 29:46.284
and that I won't accept
unless he agrees to my terms.

29:46.367 --> 29:48.161
What in the world are you thinking?

29:48.661 --> 29:50.580
You used to never take jobs like this.

29:51.331 --> 29:53.833
But you're gonna find the killer for him
all of a sudden?

29:54.334 --> 29:56.377
I have a few questions I want answered.

30:00.340 --> 30:01.382
[disconnect tone]

30:18.024 --> 30:20.026
[wistful music playing]

30:55.103 --> 30:56.354
[tires squeal]

31:02.819 --> 31:04.279
[stirring music playing]

31:06.823 --> 31:08.324
[women laughing]

31:28.970 --> 31:30.972
[stirring music continues]

32:59.477 --> 33:01.479
[panting]

33:03.106 --> 33:04.857
- [gasps]
- [music fades]

33:05.608 --> 33:07.068
Why are you following me?

33:11.739 --> 33:14.242
You must be up to no good
if you can't answer, huh?

33:16.452 --> 33:18.037
Why don't we face each other first?

33:18.997 --> 33:20.581
You move, you get hurt.

33:23.501 --> 33:24.669
Do you know an Oh Ki-hoon?

33:25.712 --> 33:26.838
You a detective?

33:26.921 --> 33:28.548
No, I wouldn't say that.

33:30.341 --> 33:32.510
I'm only looking for the person
who murdered Oh Ki-hoon.

33:33.177 --> 33:35.430
Well, it wasn't me. You guessed wrong.

33:35.513 --> 33:37.056
So then, why were you there?

33:39.017 --> 33:40.518
It was you I fought, right?

33:42.937 --> 33:44.522
I'm right, aren't I?

33:46.816 --> 33:48.818
[tender piano music playing]

34:15.720 --> 34:17.013
[Ho-jae grunts]

34:20.183 --> 34:21.601
[Ho-jae grunts, groans]

34:28.274 --> 34:29.484
[Ho-jae grunts]

34:32.028 --> 34:33.988
[Ho-jae panting]

34:34.072 --> 34:36.074
["Time" by Baek A playing]

34:37.617 --> 34:40.119
[breathing heavily]

34:45.166 --> 34:47.168
[chuckles softly]

34:53.549 --> 34:55.009
That's quite a punch you got.

34:57.553 --> 34:59.055
You're a pro, aren't you?

35:06.270 --> 35:07.730
I'm not gonna go easy on you now.

35:07.814 --> 35:09.816
This time, I won't hold back.

35:17.532 --> 35:18.366
What?

35:26.040 --> 35:27.625
Why are you looking at me like that?

35:30.920 --> 35:32.004
Master Jang.

35:32.088 --> 35:35.466
[high-pitched squeal]

35:35.550 --> 35:41.180
♪ Will it come when spring comes…? ♪

35:41.264 --> 35:42.598
Is it really you?

35:42.682 --> 35:46.853
♪ Before the cherry blossoms fall… ♪

35:46.936 --> 35:49.105
After all this time, you're still here.

35:49.188 --> 35:52.650
♪ Melting the painful times ♪

36:29.187 --> 36:34.734
♪ Will it come when winter’s gone? ♪

36:35.568 --> 36:42.450
♪ Will it come when spring comes? ♪

36:42.533 --> 36:46.954
♪ Before the cherry blossoms fall ♪

36:47.538 --> 36:52.418
♪ Melting the painful times… ♪

37:15.608 --> 37:16.734
[man] Interesting.

37:46.806 --> 37:47.807
[Chae-ok] Very soon,

37:49.100 --> 37:51.102
the cherry blossoms will be in bloom.

37:58.317 --> 37:59.652
[music fades]

38:00.611 --> 38:02.613
[pensive music playing]

38:07.368 --> 38:09.203
[automated voice] The doors are opening.

38:15.084 --> 38:19.088
WE HAVE ALWAYS BEEN CURIOUS
ABOUT HUMANS

38:19.171 --> 38:22.925
HUMANS, CREATORS OF HISTORY
AND HISTORY ITSELF

38:23.009 --> 38:25.553
THE RECORD OF EXISTENCE

38:28.264 --> 38:29.932
THE RECORD OF EXISTENCE
BY SHIN JI-OH

38:30.016 --> 38:33.436
THE BOOK OF EVOLUTION AND COEXISTENCE

38:33.519 --> 38:36.105
A FUTURE INSPIRED BY HUMANS

38:36.188 --> 38:38.691
A FUTURE BRED FOR HUMANS

38:39.191 --> 38:40.443
WE ADVANCE

38:40.526 --> 38:42.194
AND EVOLVE

38:42.278 --> 38:44.363
ENDLESSLY

38:44.864 --> 38:46.657
THE POTENTIAL OF HUMANS

38:46.741 --> 38:48.993
THE INFINITY OF HUMANKIND

38:55.958 --> 38:57.293
[music fades]

38:59.170 --> 39:01.172
[stirring music playing]

39:35.915 --> 39:37.041
[machine beeps]

39:38.918 --> 39:40.920
[eerie thrumming music playing]

39:44.548 --> 39:46.550
[dramatic music playing]

40:15.496 --> 40:16.914
[music subsides]

40:18.416 --> 40:20.418
[unsettling music playing]

40:37.726 --> 40:38.811
Let us begin.

40:40.020 --> 40:40.855
Yes, sir.

40:41.689 --> 40:44.442
We'll begin Experiment A0-67.

40:44.525 --> 40:46.527
[reverential music playing]

41:05.588 --> 41:07.381
[breathing shakily]

41:11.260 --> 41:13.471
[metallic clattering]

41:13.554 --> 41:15.639
[unsettling music playing]

41:37.286 --> 41:39.288
[squelching]

41:45.753 --> 41:47.755
[tense percussive music playing]

41:51.050 --> 41:52.635
[music swells]

41:52.718 --> 41:54.720
[music subsides]

41:55.638 --> 41:57.640
[squelching]

42:00.976 --> 42:02.603
[dramatic music playing]

43:38.991 --> 43:40.659
[music fades]

43:41.619 --> 43:43.787
["Dawn" by Kim A Reum playing]

44:06.018 --> 44:08.479
♪ Walking down the road ♪

44:09.021 --> 44:10.773
♪ Where the darkness falls ♪

44:10.856 --> 44:13.651
♪ I see the truth ♪

44:13.734 --> 44:17.529
♪ That lead us through the ebb and tide ♪

44:17.613 --> 44:20.574
♪ Our souls will blend ♪

44:20.658 --> 44:24.662
♪ Love that never fades
And never cease ♪

44:25.454 --> 44:28.290
♪ All right, all right, all right ♪

44:28.374 --> 44:30.334
♪ In your embrace ♪

44:30.417 --> 44:32.586
[music fades]
